{"seq":27,"trial_id":"v03-installer-dev-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-told-mu-v03-dev/sy-03-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-10-30T15:33:52.919Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"c749e9042466b54e0946c881746ab30455c908f69454f098f6b1dbb2584c1aa0","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03INS0001","text":"Pree, I found two Marrow Fieldworks ticket numbers:\n\n- **PD-5302**: Hollis posted in #central-random on Oct 14 that it's the Marrow Fieldworks follow-up ticket from this week, and no action is needed.\n- **#4409** and **#4412**: Moss's \"Central handoffs next week\" digest (Jan 2, 2026, in the team-central digests). They sit under the Marrow Fieldworks handoff bullet as pre-handoff items on your dealer account. #4409 is the Gatehouse Check-In timeout at the Salina North yard, and #4412 is the driver SMS prompt glitch on the overflow lots. The digest is from January, so check whether they're still open.\n\nI found nothing new in #central-team this week, and nothing in #help-it-ops or #inc-tansley-carrier-api. I couldn't open any notes under Moss's member folder with my access, so the digest is the only Moss document I could check.\n\nI left out a few numbers that look similar but don't belong to Marrow Fieldworks:\n- PD-4821 and FR-882 are for Marrow Agrisupply.\n- #88412 is for Tansleigh Packaging.\n- #8841 is on Tobias's Plains depot work, and the message doesn't name the account."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03INS0001","ts":"1792159200.000126"}}
